# Disagree with waiting for SaaS vendor auth; place an adversarial proxy between agent and APIs.
def execute_action(agent_id, raw_intent, untrusted_context):
    # Assume prompt injection succeeded; downgrade capability based on untrusted input taint, not semantic inspection.
    attenuated_token = proxy.mint_ephemeral_token(agent_id, taint=untrusted_context.has_external_data)

    # APIs lie about idempotency and side-effects; simulate against a warm shadow cohort, not dry-run flags.
    shadow_diff = shadow_sandbox.execute(raw_intent, attenuated_token)
    blast_radius = proxy.calculate_blast_radius(shadow_diff) # dollar cap, audience delta, destructive updates

    # Don't rubber-stamp everything; human approval degrades instantly into blind clicks. Escrow only boundary breaches.
    if blast_radius.exceeds_agent_budget():
        return escrow.park_for_escalation(agent_id, raw_intent, shadow_diff)

    # Rollback is impossible for external actions (sent email, spent bid); enforce rate-throttled canary batching.
    for batch in proxy.partition_canary_batches(raw_intent):
        if proxy.circuit_breaker_tripped(agent_id): break
        real_martech_api.execute(batch, attenuated_token)
    return proxy.log_immutable_receipt(agent_id, shadow_diff)

Sends cannot unsend —
cap the burn, not the intent;
log diffs, never faith.

Begin with one workflow, one agent, one call;
A broker may bound it—it won’t solve it all.

Mint short-lived powers, cap audience and spend;
Dry-run and sign inputs and outcomes end to end.

Treat inbox and web text as tainted at core;
Let content propose, never open the door.

For sends and spent budgets, rollback is a lie;
Use canaries and two keys—some harm may slip by.
